---

<DocsLayout
  title="Read implementation status before API shape."
  description="StateKnot is pre-alpha: AgentService v1 and one strict MCP Remote Tool profile now join the durable provider-native path; stable network APIs, broader MCP/A2A, advanced graph semantics, and production qualification remain unfinished."
  section="Implementation status"
>
  <section aria-labelledby="status-matrix-title">
    <h2 id="status-matrix-title">Capability matrix</h2>
    <ul class="status-list">
      {
        capabilities.map((capability) => (
          <li class="status-item">
            <span class:list={["status-badge", capability.className]}>
              {capability.state}
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3>{capability.title}</h3>
              <p>{capability.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="claim-title">
    <h2 id="claim-title">What “implemented” means</h2>
    <p>
      Code and executable tests exist in the repository. It does not mean the
      API is stable, the crate is published, operational release gates pass, or
      compatibility support has started. A v1 capability is supported only when
      implementation, tests, documentation, compatibility evidence, and release
      gates ship together.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="next-proof-title">
    <h2 id="next-proof-title">The next proof boundary</h2>
    <p>
      AgentService v1 now proves authorization-first submission/read/cancel
      semantics, and the strict MCP binding proves modern discovery, exact
      identity/schema pins, attempt credentials, and ambiguous lost-write
      mapping. The next proof boundary composes that adapter with the PostgreSQL
      invocation ledger and crash recovery, then publishes the pinned official
      MCP conformance report. A2A follows only after this narrower protocol
      profile has end-to-end durable evidence.
    </p>
  </section>

